meta {
  name: POST Ingest Signal (BUY bracket — SL+TP)
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/webhook/{{indianWebhookToken}}
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "action": "BUY",
    "symbol": "RELIANCE",
    "lot": 1,
    "sl_pts": 20,
    "tp_pts": 30,
    "order_type": "MARKET",
    "comment": "bruno_bracket"
  }
}

docs {
  Bracket/cover order signal. Requires an Indian broker credential (Zerodha/Angel/Dhan)
  or MT5, using whichever webhook token that credential is bound to
  (`indianWebhookToken` in this collection — see Webhooks → create-indian,
  configured `default_order_type: MARKET`, so `order_type` here must match).

  Broker behaviour under BROKER_MODE=mock: passes through as normal market order;
  trade record will show `order_type: bracket` regardless.

  Live broker behaviour:
  - Zerodha (MIS): Cover Order via POST /orders/co; TP is ignored (CO only supports SL).
  - Angel (MIS):   ROBO order via placeOrder; both SL and TP applied.
  - Dhan (any):    Rejected with error_code=bracket_not_supported.
  - MT5:           stopLoss / takeProfit added to MetaApi trade payload.

  CNC product guard: bracket orders on CNC/delivery product are always rejected with
  error_code=bracket_not_supported regardless of broker.

  Check GET /v1/webhooks/:id/trades:
  - `order_type`: "bracket"
  - `sl_price`:   absolute SL price computed from LTP (Indian) or ask/bid (MT5)
  - `tp_price`:   absolute TP price (null for Zerodha CO)
}

tests {
  test("Status 202 queued", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(202);
    expect(res.getBody().queued).to.equal(true);
  });
}
